  :status :draft
  :body
  {:hook
   "Choose `g(x)=x⁻¹ᐟ²`: it is integrable, its square is the borderline nonintegrable `x⁻¹`, and its entropy can be dominated by the slightly stronger but integrable power `4x⁻³ᐟ⁴`."
   :how-to-apply
   ["Define `g x` by `x^(-1/2)` for `x > 0` and zero otherwise, keeping measurability and endpoint behavior explicit."
    "Use `integrableOn_Ioo_rpow_iff` to prove `g ∈ L¹(0,1)` and to refute integrability of `g² = x⁻¹`."
    "Define the entropy density `ent x = g x * log (g x)`."
    "Apply `Real.abs_log_mul_self_rpow_lt` with exponent `1/4` and factor the powers to obtain `|ent x| ≤ 4x⁻³ᐟ⁴` on `(0,1)`."
    "Use the integrability of `x⁻³ᐟ⁴` to prove the entropy integral is finite."
    "Derive the pointwise Young–Fenchel inequality `g*f ≤ exp f + g*log g` from `Real.add_one_le_exp (f - log g)`."
    "Set `A = ∫ ent + 2`; combine the admissibility bound `∫ exp f ≤ 1` with integral monotonicity, avoiding an unnecessary exact evaluation of the entropy integral."]
